# Hetzner host-local disk check — user-crontab entry for the Hetzner box.
#
# The disk check MUST run on Hetzner itself (it pages for Hetzner disks).
# Install (once, as your normal user — no root needed):
#   ./monitors/install-hetzner-disk-check.sh
# which appends the line below to your crontab if missing.
#
# Cadence: EVERY 5 MINUTES (Europe/Berlin wall clock via TZ prefix is not
# portable in user crontabs; the script logs UTC timestamps).
# The cron entry points at the STABLE installed copy
# (/usr/local/sbin/hetzner-disk-check.sh) — never at a worktree path, so the
# pager survives worktree retirement. Re-run install-hetzner-disk-check.sh
# after pulling script updates.

# */5 * * * * /usr/local/sbin/hetzner-disk-check.sh >> /home/alexey/.local/state/hetzner-disk-check/cron.log 2>&1
